meta {
  name: Cancel a loan
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/loans/{{loanId}}/cancel
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "Reader changed their mind"
  }
}

docs {
  200. The row stays and moves to Cancelled - a state deliberately distinct from Returned,
  because a cancelled loan is not one the reader ever fulfilled and the history has to be
  able to say which of the two happened months later.

  The body is optional: a cancellation with no reason is ordinary, and sending none is a 200
  rather than a 400. The reason is recorded on the audit entry, truncated rather than
  trusted to be short.

  409 if the loan was already returned or cancelled - and the message names which of the two
  it actually is rather than a generic conflict. Run this after "Return a copy" in a folder
  run and that is exactly what you will see.
}
